        "content": "Two groups of documents answer the same question. Say how the two answers relate. Do not say which one is right.\n\nQuestion: What is the estimated total population of Moyale?\n\nAnswer A: 13,962\n  about: Moyale\n  sense: 1994 Ethiopian census\n  as of: 1994\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: Ethiopian census\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The 1994 Ethiopian census reported that the Ethiopian side of Moyale had a total population of 13,962, of whom 7,411 were men and 6,551 were women.\" [document 4]\n\nAnswer B: 66,495\n  about: Moyale\n  sense: 1994 national census\n  as of: 1994\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: the 1994 national census\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The 1994 national census reported a total population for this woreda of 66,495, of whom 35,048 were men and 31,411 women;\" [document 5]; \"The 1994 national census reported a total population for this woreda of 66,495 , of whom 35,048 were men and 31,411 women ;\" [document 6]\n\nExplanation found in the documents: \"The 1994 Ethiopian census reported that the Ethiopian side of Moyale had a total population of 13,962, of whom 7,411 were men and 6,551 were women. (This total also includes an estimate for parts of the town of Moyale, which were not counted; for these parts of the town, it was estimated there were 3,419 inhabitants, of whom 1,752 were men and 1,667 were women.)\" [document 1]\n\nThe relations:\n- \"agree\": the same answer, possibly at another precision or in other words.\n- \"different entity\": the answers are about different things that share a name.\n- \"different sense\": the same entity, but a different event, edition, version, condition, place or measure.\n- \"different time\": the same entity and sense; the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\n- \"complementary\": both are true, and together they form a fuller answer.\n- \"opinion\": judgments, recommendations or contested findings, on which sources may fairly differ.\n- \"contradiction\": the same entity, sense and time; both cannot be true, and nothing explains the difference.\n\nGo only by what is shown for each answer. Choose \"different entity\", \"different sense\" or \"different time\" only when the identifying details, senses or dates shown really differ, or the explanation shows it; do not assume a difference that is not stated. If the answers are about the same thing in the same sense and cannot both be true, it is a contradiction.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"relation\": \"\"}"
